THIS DIRECTORY IS NOT APACHE-2.0.

Every file in src/backend/enterprise/frameworks is a COMMERCIAL ADD-ON MODULE
of Correlix. It implements the `security_dialects` entitlement — whose locked
scope is device-hardening dialects beyond the default set AND compliance
frameworks beyond the default two — which the owner has placed in the
Enterprise tier. What lives here is the CROSSWALK content for NIST CSF 2.0,
the HIPAA §164.312 technical safeguards and PCI DSS v4.0.1.

The rest of Correlix is Apache-2.0. The projection engine, the owned 800-53
control catalogue, the framework VOCABULARY (ids, descriptors, versions, the
default set and the closed list an API write is validated against) and the two
default frameworks — NIST SP 800-53 Rev5 and CIS Controls v8.1 — are core
(src/backend/internal/compliancemodel) and are unaffected by this notice.

With this directory deleted the product still runs: all five frameworks stay in
the catalogue and stay selectable, a stored selection is still valid, and an
enabled framework whose crosswalk is gone reports a NULL score with a sentence
saying the crosswalk is not included in this deployment — never an empty
scorecard that would read as a clean bill.

